# Copy to docker/.env (never commit the real file) before `docker compose up`.
#
# The connector itself needs no secrets here. Everything below is connectors-bundle's own
# connection to your Camunda SaaS cluster.
#
# Create the API client in Camunda Console (your cluster -> API -> create client) with the
# "Orchestration Cluster API" scope (Orchestration Cluster REST API + Zeebe gRPC) AND the
# "Secrets" scope (Administration API, Secrets resource) - the Secrets scope is what lets this
# self-hosted runtime read the GOVERNOR_PRICE_TABLE cluster secret from Console; without it the
# token request for audience secrets.camunda.io is refused with HTTP 401. Optimize API is not
# needed. Cluster ID and region are shown in the cluster's details / the client credentials block.

CAMUNDA_CLUSTER_ID=
CAMUNDA_CLUSTER_REGION=
CAMUNDA_CLIENT_ID=
CAMUNDA_CLIENT_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL - only if the runtime logs "Failed with code 404" when fetching a process definition
# (health shows processDefinitionImport DOWN). Newer clusters serve the REST API at
# https://<region>.api.camunda.io/<cluster-id> rather than the runtime's built-in default
# https://<region>.zeebe.camunda.io/<cluster-id>. Leave commented out otherwise.
# CAMUNDA_CLIENT_REST_ADDRESS=https://your-region.api.camunda.io/your-cluster-id

# OPTIONAL - log level for the connector's own log lines. INFO (default) = one summary line per
# call; DEBUG = also the inputs, the price-table decision and the rates used.
# GOVERNOR_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
